NAME: Morning brief
OWNER: TMEC Command
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday at 6:17 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Morning brief" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Morning brief · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Morning brief · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Morning brief · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Morning brief · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Morning brief · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Use the morning-brief skill. Read yesterday's and today's notes from every bot in /workspace/tmec-team/daily/, every item in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/, yesterday's and today's lines in the run log, and /workspace/tmec-team/data/ops/capacity.md. Send Tommy one brief under 200 words: first the numbered items waiting on his yes (at most 7, oldest first, each one line with who it goes to), then one line per bot (what it did, with the number and where it came from; "no run" if it has no log line; UNKNOWN if its source failed), then the capacity line. On Mondays add Forecast's scoreboard summary. This brief always goes out, even when everything is quiet. Save it to /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/brief.md and put it at the top of /workspace/tmec-team/vault/Daily/<today>.md.
